Sorting command line arguments in C++


Sorting command line arguments is a common task. Here is a simple way to do it using the standard library's `sort` function.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <algorithm> // For std::sort
#include <vector>    // For std::vector

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    std::vector<int> args; // Store command line arguments in a vector

    // Copy command line arguments to vector
    for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i) {
        args.push_back(std::stoi(argv[i])); // Convert string to integer
    }

