```csharp
public class HtmlLabelRenderer : LabelRenderer
{
    protected override void OnElementChanged(ElementChangedEventArgs<Label> e)
    {
        base.OnElementChanged(e);

        if (Control != null)
        {
            var html = ((HtmlLabel)e.Element).Html;
            var parser = new HtmlAgilityPack.HtmlDocument();
            parser.LoadHtml(html);
            var nodes = parser.DocumentNode.SelectNodes("//*/text()");

            foreach (var node in nodes)
            {
                Control.Text += node.InnerText;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This custom renderer will parse the HTML and update the `Control.Text` property accordingly. You can use this renderer in your Android project and set the `Html` property of your `Label` to the desired HTML content. Note that this is a workaround and may have performance implications, especially for complex HTML.

