It's not thread safe. Writes to the context class variable are not guaranteed to be visible to threads that read that variable through getContext(). At the very least, declare context to be volatile. Ideally, redefine context as an AtomicReference, set through a call like this:

if(!context.compareAndSet(null, theContext))
