Here is how you can pass a list of strings as a parameter in Cucumber io.cucumber 6.x:

First, define a method to parse the string into a list of strings:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;

public class StringListParser {

    public static List<String> parseStringToList(String input) {
        return Arrays.asList(input.split(",\\s?"));
    }
}
```

Then, use this method in your step definition:

```java
import io.cucumber.java.Before;
import io.cucumber.java.Scenario;
import io.cucumber.java.Step;
import io.cucumber.java.After;

public class YourFeatureFile {

    @Before
    public void beforeScenario(Scenario scenario) {
        StringListParser.setInstance(new StringListParser());
    }

    @After
    public void afterScenario(Scenario scenario) {
        StringListParser.setInstance(null);
    }

    @Step("^a list of strings \"(.+?)\"$")
    public void a_list_of_strings(String input) {
        List<String> list = StringListParser.parseStringToList(input);
        System.out.println(list);
    }
}
```

In the `beforeScenario` hook, we set `StringListParser` as the instance to be used

